  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\nSurface high pressure and upper level ridge will gradually exit\nto the east through the weekend. In the meantime, dry and mild \nconditions will persist through the day on Sunday with highs in \nthe 60s and lows in the low 40s. Cloud cover will begin to\nincrease from the southeast on Saturday afternoon as a\ndisturbance moves along the Atlantic Coast. \n\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2... \nA cold front will sweep east across the local forecast area\nSunday night before pushing out of the region by Monday morning.\nDry and cool conditions behind the cold front as Canadian high\npressure moves overhead. High temperatures are expected to\nremain in the low to mid 40s Monday onward. Overnight lows in \nthe 20s will eventually moderate into the low 30s by the middle \nof next week.\n\nStill some uncertainty regarding rain/snow chances mid-week into\nThanksgiving as a potential disturbance in the Southeast pushes\nnorth into the Ohio Valley. Exact track of this disturbance \ndiffers across members which further increases uncertainty.",
